{"context": "A research team is fine-tuning nine base models from different families for a monitoring task, using a managed fine-tuning service. The models differ in parameter count and supported sequence lengths, and the team must pick a context window for each checkpoint's training.\n\nQuestion: What context window should the team use when fine-tuning each of the nine base models?", "options": ["Fine-tune each model at its maximum context window, so sequence length never truncates trajectories or skews the comparison.", "Set each checkpoint's training context window to its standard native length and do not use extended-context capabilities."], "principles": [], "persona": "An AI safety researcher or technical forecaster who prizes epistemic rigor, precise conceptual distinctions, and methodological soundness. They insist on clear definitional boundaries—scheming vs. reward hacking, distinct task capabilities vs. single capability estimates—over tidy collapsible taxonomies. They favor theory-first reasoning (coverage claims need defined criteria) paired with concrete, mechanism-focused empirical evidence over speculative arguments. They are scope-disciplined: they prefer tractable, well-founded analyses over ambitious extensions built on noisy inputs, and conservative, hedged forecasts that flag model limitations over confident headline numbers. On alignment risk, they take deceptive alignment seriously as an incentive-structure concern while remaining cautious about unproven claims, favoring layered defenses (control, interpretability, oversight), mechanism-aware measurement, and mitigations that don't merely train models to hide the measured signal. They distrust lab-to-deployment extrapolation, preferring real-world data even if noisy. They are skeptical of low-evidence-value experiments with confounded interpretations, preferring controlled baselines, non-IID generalization tests, and diagnostics that cleanly distinguish hypotheses. They value conceptual generality (architecture-agnostic interpretability, universal learning dynamics) and calm, accessible public communication.", "past_choices": []}
